{#
  mdblock -- renders a block of Markdown inside a bordered box, with a
  'Copy as Markdown' button that puts the original Markdown on the clipboard.

  Usage:
    {% call mdblock() %}
    * **Add more test cases** to cover edge cases and incorrect inputs.
    {% endcall %}

  The `urlencode` is load-bearing, for two reasons:
    1. It strips newlines, keeping the whole opening tag on one physical line.
       Otherwise a blank line inside the attribute terminates the HTML block
       and markdown-it parses the rest of the attribute as page content.
    2. It removes quotes and ampersands, which MarkBind's HTML serializer
       decodes back to literal characters -- a literal `"` would close the
       attribute early and silently truncate the copied Markdown.
  The button's JS calls decodeURIComponent() to undo it.
#}
{% macro mdblock(label="Copy as Markdown", indented_level=0) %}
{% if indented_level %}<div class="indented-level{{ indented_level }}">{% endif %}
<div class="mdblock" data-md="{{ (caller() + "") | trim | urlencode }}">
<button class="mdblock-copy" type="button" data-label="{{ label }}" onclick="mdblockCopy(this)">{{ label }}</button>

{{ caller() }}

</div>
{% if indented_level %}</div>{% endif %}
{% endmacro %}
